      "text": "Hi, how are you holding up?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 11.15,
      "end": 16.07,
      "text": "That's stick drift, and it's sadly very common. Is the controller still under warranty?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 20.83,
      "end": 27.15,
      "text": "Some manufacturers still repair drift for free, so it's worth checking their support page. If not, you have a few options."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 31.53,
      "end": 40.62,
      "text": "You can increase the dead zone in the game settings if it's mild. Some people clean around the stick with a little electronics cleaner. Or you can buy a replacement stick module and swap it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 50.28,
      "end": 58.95,
      "text": "It involves a tiny screwdriver and sometimes soldering, so it's not for everyone. If you're nervous, a local repair shop can usually do it for less than a new controller."
